<!--Post: 10441--><!--Time: 1109961360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10441"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 10:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If Dennis the Menace was smart he&#39;d realize he&#39;s much safer IN the pokey than out. If he escapes he officially becomes FAIR GAME.  <BR> <BR>I lived in Michigan&#39;s Upper Peninsula for a while In Marquette, home of the meanest evilist &#40;to quote Arlo Guthrie--&#34;Father rapers&#34;&#41; dudes around in Marquette State Prison ---ie John Norman Collins &#40;now Chapman&#41;, the Co-Ed killer. <BR> <BR>When the local media would come on and say &#40;and it was rare&#41; that someone had escaped the prison, all the locals &#40;known as Yoopers&#41; would take out with their hunting rifles and tracking dogs going looking for the &#39;reeee-ward&#39;. <BR> <BR> <BR>Dennis should be so lucky<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10441-->
<!--Post: 10492--><!--Time: 1109972989-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10492"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Witchking, <BR> <BR>How far off in fantasy land are you ? Everyone has had 30yrs to catch Radar. The worse place Radar could be in is prison right now. His case carries huge notoriety. He is a huge target in prison for assasination by inmates, gangs, or rogue guards looking to add to their reputations. <BR> <BR>If Radar was released he would elude a bunch of &#34;townies&#34; without a problem. But inside, even in isolation, he will have to watch his back every second he is outside his isolation cell.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10492-->
<!--Post: 10537--><!--Time: 1109987575-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10537"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 5:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Witchking, I grew up in the Upper Peninsula and we had a minimusm security prison near where I lived. They would have frequent &#39;walk-aways&#39; but never for long. Most of the incarerated were from cities and if they escaped they found out they were deathly afaid of bears and very susseptible to being eaten alive by something even worse, mosquitos. They would find their way back or would have someone call the prison to come and get them. I don&#39;t think anyone ever actually escaped.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10537-->
<!--Post: 10546--><!--Time: 1109996187-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10546"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 8:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey, Denny, come out to play.....some of my heavy hittin&#39;, pipe swingin&#39; bro&#39;s from K.C. are heading down to give you a &#34;ride.&#34;   <BR> <BR>FYI Love the red jumpsuit.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
